;; The module marshal (PY6b, the import family): a port of CPython 3.14's Python/marshal.c, versions 0 to 5,
;; dumps, loads, dump and load with allow_code, references (version 3 on), interned strings (sys.intern's
;; table, internStr), sets in the order of their elements' dumps (bpo-37596) and the errors' messages.
;; Two differences from CPython, both of its object model: an object is written with FLAG_REF whenever
;; references are on (CPython leaves out an object its reference count says is not shared; pyi has no
;; counts), so the bytes differ in that bit and every object read is kept in the reference list, which
;; loads either way; and a code object is pyi's (its IR, not CPython's bytecode): TYPE_CODE with CPython's
;; fields, co_code holding pyi's instructions (marshal_code.go), so CPython's .pyc code is refused and
;; pyi's own .pyc files carry their own magic number (_imp.pyc_magic_number_token).

